<title>FRANCE: EU grants free-market wheat, barley, rye, oats.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-market wheat, barley, rye, oats.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following export licences for free-market grain, grain traders said. The refunds agreed by the EU's cereals management committee in Brussels are in Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>			   Tonnage	   Maximum refund</p>
<p>MAIN TENDER</p>
<p>    Soft wheat	 332,500		 6.90</p>
<p>    Barley		63,500		31.00</p>
<p>    Rye		    5,150		30.09</p>
<p>    Oats		  22,000		30.59</p>
<p>TENDER FOR EXPORT TO ACP COUNTRIES</p>
<p>			    Tonnage	     Max refund</p>
<p>    Soft wheat	  21,000		12.00</p>
<p>Member country officials later confirmed these figures.</p>
<p>The award of 332,500 tonnes of free-market soft wheat was the largest wheat award made by the EU since the campaign started on July 1.</p>
<p>It exceeded a previous peak of 311,650 tonnes of free-market wheat awarded on October 3.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
